  "date": "mayo de 1528",
  "vocab": [
    { "id": "agua", "es": "agua", "en": "water", "pos": "noun", "note": "el agua, but feminine: el agua fría, las aguas." },
    { "id": "balsa", "es": "balsa", "en": "raft", "pos": "noun", "note": "la balsa. A raft; also the tree that gives balsa wood." },
    { "id": "maiz", "es": "maíz", "en": "corn", "pos": "noun", "cognate": true, "note": "el maíz. Maize. Stress the í: ma-ÍZ." },
    { "id": "guia", "es": "guía", "en": "guide", "pos": "noun", "cognate": true, "note": "el guía for the person; la guía is a guidebook." },
    { "id": "campo", "es": "campo", "en": "field", "pos": "noun", "cognate": true, "note": "el campo. A field, or the countryside. Think camp." },
    { "id": "corriente", "es": "corriente", "en": "current", "pos": "noun", "cognate": true, "note": "la corriente." }
  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    [
      "The ",
      { "id": "rio", "es": "río", "en": "river" },
      " is wide and the ",
      { "id": "corriente", "es": "corriente", "en": "current" },
      " is strong. There is no ford. The ",
      { "id": "hombre", "es": "hombres", "en": "men" },
      " who can swim, swim. The rest cut ",
      { "id": "pino", "es": "pinos", "en": "pines" },
      " and tie them into ",
      { "id": "balsa", "es": "balsas", "en": "rafts" },
      ", and the ",
      { "id": "balsa", "es": "balsas", "en": "rafts" },
      " turn in the ",
      { "id": "corriente", "es": "corriente", "en": "current" },
      " and the horses go across with their heads up and their eyes white. It takes a whole day. At the end of it we are on the other side, wet, with the same ",
      { "id": "hambre", "es": "hambre", "en": "hunger" },
      "."
    ],
    [
      "On the far bank, in the evening, up to two hundred Indians come out of the trees. I count what I can see. They are big ",
      { "id": "hombre", "es": "hombres", "en": "men" },
      " and they carry bows. The ",
      { "id": "gobernador", "es": "gobernador", "en": "governor" },
      " walks toward them. They make signs, and the signs are the signs from the beach: go away. Our ",
      { "id": "hombre", "es": "hombres", "en": "men" },
      " take five or six of them. This is how we get ",
      { "id": "guia", "es": "guías", "en": "guides" },
      " in this ",
      { "id": "tierra", "es": "tierra", "en": "land" },
      ". We take them."
    ],
    [
      "The ",
      { "id": "guia", "es": "guías", "en": "guides" },
      " lead us half a league to their houses, and around the houses there is ",
      { "id": "maiz", "es": "maíz", "en": "corn" },
      ". ",
      { "id": "campo", "es": "Campos", "en": "Fields" },
      " of ",
      { "id": "maiz", "es": "maíz", "en": "corn" },
      ", ripe, ready to be picked. I have seen soldiers weep at less. The ",
      { "id": "hombre", "es": "hombres", "en": "men" },
      " go into the ",
      { "id": "campo", "es": "campos", "en": "fields" },
      " and eat it raw, and the ",
      { "id": "gobernador", "es": "gobernador", "en": "governor" },
      " lets them, and then orders it gathered. That night there is ",
      { "id": "comida", "es": "comida", "en": "food" },
      ". There is ",
      { "id": "maiz", "es": "maíz", "en": "corn" },
      " roasted in the fires, and ",
      { "id": "agua", "es": "agua", "en": "water" },
      " from the ",
      { "id": "rio", "es": "río", "en": "river" },
      ", and for the first time since the ships nobody talks about the ships."
    ],
    [
      "I sit by the ",
      { "id": "agua", "es": "agua", "en": "water" },
      " and count. Fifteen days of ",
      { "id": "arena", "es": "arena", "en": "sand" },
      " for one ",
      { "id": "campo", "es": "campo", "en": "field" },
      " of ",
      { "id": "maiz", "es": "maíz", "en": "corn" },
      ". A ",
      { "id": "guia", "es": "guía", "en": "guide" },
      " is a ",
      { "id": "hombre", "es": "hombre", "en": "man" },
      " we have taken by force, who will lead us where he wants, and we will follow, because we have no other way to ask. The ",
      { "id": "corriente", "es": "corriente", "en": "current" },
      " is loud all night. Somewhere down it there is the ",
      { "id": "mar", "es": "mar", "en": "sea" },
      ", and somewhere on the ",
      { "id": "mar", "es": "mar", "en": "sea" },
      " there are our ships, looking for a harbor we told them to find."
    ],
    [
      "In the morning the ",
      { "id": "guia", "es": "guías", "en": "guides" },
      " walk at the front and our ",
      { "id": "hombre", "es": "hombres", "en": "men" },
      " walk close behind them. The ",
      { "id": "campo", "es": "campos", "en": "fields" },
      " of ",
      { "id": "maiz", "es": "maíz", "en": "corn" },
      " fall behind us, and the ",
      { "id": "agua", "es": "agua", "en": "water" },
      " we carry is the only thing that is heavier than it was."
    ]
  ],
